Good Morning, Jose,

 

My name is Michael Kotson, and I am a Cybersecurity researcher at MIT
Lincoln Laboratory.  I am developing a lecture for an internal class on
phishing and social engineering for Lincoln staff, and I am hoping to
include a machine learning-based exercise to illustrate the differences
between detecting phishing attacks and run-of-the-mill spam.

 

If your Phishing Corpus from 2007 is still available, would you mind if I
used it for this class?  Or do you have suggestions for other datasets that
might suit our needs?

 

Thank you very much for your time, and I hope you have a wonderful day.

 

Regards,

 

Michael

 

----------------------------------------- 

Michael C. Kotson

Associate Staff
MIT Lincoln Laboratory

Cyber Systems and Operations

michael.kotson@ll.mit.edu

